      "id": 1,
      "text": "Silver Lake was platted in 1881 and named for the lake that sits on its northern shore.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_Lake%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The area around the glacial lake drew pioneers in the 1850s, attracted by fertile prairies, timbered Big Woods, and the South Fork of the Crow River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/silver_lake_minnesota",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Railroad plans in the 1880s spurred Silver Lake's growth, turning a slow‑growing village into a thriving community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/silver_lake_minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Silver Lake became a farming hub settled mainly by Bohemian and Polish immigrants who built churches, mills, and creameries in the late 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/silver_lake_minnesota",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Silver Lake was incorporated as a village in 1889, eight years after its 1881 platting.",
